      "file": "scenes/scene-2.js",
      "narration": "Think in roles, not favourite colours. A background, text, a couple of greys, one accent for what matters and a quiet support colour. That's five to seven in total.",
      "storyboard": "Paper-white stage, wide shot. Empty labelled slots fill one by one as each role is spoken: background, text, two greys, then on 'one accent' a coral swatch drops in with a small bounce, and on 'quiet support' a blue swatch slides in smaller. On 'five to seven' a bracket draws across the row with the count '5\u20137' in 140px coral. Headline 'Roles, not favourites' sits top-left; bullets are rebuilt as the slot row.",
      "minDuration": 11,
      "slide": {
        "title": "Think in Roles, Not Favourite Colours",
        "text": "Background and text. One to two greys. One accent for what matters. One support colour, used sparingly",
        "notes": "Think in roles, not favourite colours. Pick a background, text colours, a couple of greys, one accent for what matters and a quiet support colour. That's five to seven in total.",
