    {
      "file": "scenes/scene-3.js",
      "narration": "Colours that look fine on your monitor can wash out on a projector. Aim for 4.5 to 1 contrast for body text, and label your chart series directly.",
      "storyboard": "Split stage: left a crisp monitor, right a projector beam. On 'wash out' the same text in the beam fades to a ghostly grey. On '4.5 to 1' a huge '4.5:1' slams in at 160px over the darkened text and it snaps back to legible ink. On 'label your chart series directly' a small line chart loses its legend box and names appear at each line's end. The '3:1 for large text' point is kept as a small secondary caption.",
      "minDuration": 11,
      "slide": {
        "title": "Test Contrast Before You Commit",
        "text": "4.5:1 for normal text. 3:1 for large text and graphics. Check accent on background. Add direct labels to charts",
        "notes": "Colours that look fine on your monitor can wash out on a projector. Aim for 4.5 to 1 contrast for body text, and label your chart series directly.",
